* Level 3

In Level 3, I first navigated to the Wax_jungle directory and used cd and ls -la to explore the available files and look for the clue, but I couldn't find anything useful. 
I then followed the hint provided in README.md and checked the available Git branches using git branch -a, where I found the little_garden branch. 
I switched to this branch using git switch little_garden and checked the contents again using ls -la. This time, I found three directories: sector_alpha, sector_beta, and sector_gamma. 
I then used find . -type f -name "*.log" -exec md5sum {} \; | sort | uniq -w32 -u to search through the .log files and identify the unique file containing the clue. 
Finally, I inspected the identified file using cat and found Poneglyph Fragment 1.

find . searches the current directory
-type f selects files, -name "*.log" finds .log files
-exec md5sum {} \; calculates the MD5 hash of each file
| sort sorts the results, 
uniq -w32 compares the first 32 characters


